Korean vocabulary provenance and licensing
==========================================

The vocabulary combines 49,239 natural words extracted from the first
pages-articles shard of Korean Wikipedia (2026-09-01) with 216 authored
regression inputs. 97 regression inputs were not already present, giving
49,336 unique NFC inputs in voc.txt. This is a page-ID-bounded sample, not
all of Korean Wikipedia or a balanced corpus of Korean.

Wikipedia source
----------------

Source: https://dumps.wikimedia.org/kowiki/20260901/
File: kowiki-20260901-pages-articles1.xml-p1p82407.bz2
Page ID range: 1 through 82407
Mirror: https://dumps.wikimedia.your.org/kowiki/20260901/
SHA-1: 450935900fa10ab4864b3856b54e5028c767daf0
SHA-256: 4155a5ac6dc45c7fd8b2eef471f52eedf3149d954a36535d10ae4add4a1f682c

Attribution: Korean Wikipedia contributors. The source archive contains
page titles, IDs and revision metadata. Individual contributor histories
are linked from the corresponding pages at https://ko.wikipedia.org/ and
can be reached with https://ko.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?curid=PAGE_ID&action=history.

The source text is available under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
See Wikimedia's licensing statement: https://dumps.wikimedia.org/legal.html
The derived Wikipedia vocabulary retains that license. No claim is made
that the Wikipedia material is covered by the software's BSD license.

Extraction used snowball-data commit a0ec0d0a2839ec885878868de20fcb63209d92b0:

    # Alias the filename because the extractor recognizes .xml.bz2 endings.
    ln -s kowiki-20260901-pages-articles1.xml-p1p82407.bz2 kowiki-sample.xml.bz2
    scripts/wikipedia-dump-to-freq kowiki-sample.xml.bz2 5 Hangul > korean.freq

From the resulting frequency file, retain tokens occurring at least 10
times, normalize them to NFC, retain only whole tokens consisting of 1-20
modern Hangul syllables (U+AC00 through U+D7A3), then sort by Unicode code
point and remove duplicates. Merge the regression inputs described below.
The existing extractor removes wiki markup but may retain some markup
artifacts; the list has not been exhaustively linguistically curated.

output.txt was generated from voc.txt by:

    stemwords -l korean -c UTF_8 -i korean/voc.txt -o korean/output.txt

The generated outputs are regression expectations, not independently
annotated linguistic gold labels. The experimental stemmer changes only
a small fraction of the natural vocabulary; broad recall is not claimed.

Project regression inputs
-------------------------

The 216 authored regression pairs were introduced by nethippo's Korean
Snowball contribution in commits 550790ed9799ec618a69a1a7e66bf6bddedd8763 and
5fe8444bfdfeeccbaf91909a2698d432316594f0, available at:
https://github.com/nethippo/snowball/tree/5fe8444bfdfeeccbaf91909a2698d432316594f0/tests/korean/data/korean

These cases include positive paths, ambiguous forms deliberately preserved,
and complete-word boundary checks. They were originally distributed under
the Snowball BSD 3-clause terms. The pre-existing notices below are retained;
they do not attribute the new Wikipedia dataset to the software authors.

